<title>JAPAN: Kawasaki Steel plans lower 97/98 capex.</title>
<headline>Kawasaki Steel plans lower 97/98 capex.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kawasaki Steel Corp said on Tuesday it plans parent company capital investment of 45 billion yen in the year to March 31, 1998.</p>
<p>The planned 1997/98 spending will be down 23.7 percent from an estimated 59 billion yen in 1996/97, it said.</p>
<p>The company also said its depreciation costs for 1997/98 will be 104 billion yen, down nine percent from an estimated 114.3 billion yen in 1996/97.</p>
</text>
